  "prefLabel": "Rab 303.04 Examination Deadlines",
  "priorExpiration": "2023-02-02",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Rab 303.04 Examination Deadlines. A new applicant not currently licensed or certified in another jurisdiction, shall have up to 24 months, after approval by the OPLC, to take and pass an AQB approved qualifying examination for licensure or certification. Successful completion of the examination shall be valid for a period of 24 months.\n\nSource. #9018, eff 11-1-07; ss by #10270, eff 2-2-13, EXPIRED: 2-2-23\n\nNew. #13967, eff 7-16-24 (formerly Rab 303.05) (see Revision Note at chapter heading for Rab 300)",
